WEBVTT

00:01.980 --> 00:04.310
<b>Five days prior</b>

00:02.460 --> 00:07.130
A cherry blossom tree has been planted 
to commemorate your graduation.

00:07.740 --> 00:10.990
It's only a bundle of twigs now, but 
it will have blossomed spectacularly

00:10.990 --> 00:13.490
by the time you become
fully-fledged members of society.

00:14.110 --> 00:20.900
We wish for your futures, ten, twenty 
years from now, to blossom just the same.

00:21.980 --> 00:25.130
What do cherry blossoms mean in floriography?

00:25.130 --> 00:27.820
Something about beauty of the mind, maybe?

00:28.850 --> 00:30.950
Okay, everyone, look this way.

00:31.420 --> 00:34.270
We want to take pictures 
for the grad committee.

00:34.270 --> 00:35.800
Gather a little closer.

00:37.010 --> 00:41.090
I don't think the four of us have 
ever gotten a picture together.

00:41.440 --> 00:42.770
Now that you mention it...

00:42.770 --> 00:45.050
Okay, say, "Timpani."

00:56.530 --> 01:00.450
<b>Final Episode</b>

00:56.530 --> 01:00.450
<b>Connecting Melodies</b>

01:00.450 --> 01:02.080
<b>Four days prior</b>

01:02.310 --> 01:05.530
Trombones, watch the accents.

01:05.530 --> 01:06.440
Yes.

01:06.440 --> 01:08.010
All right, once more.

01:08.010 --> 01:09.070
Yes.

01:10.000 --> 01:12.000
<b>Three days prior</b>

01:25.940 --> 01:28.780
That piece really is pretty.

01:31.090 --> 01:33.980
It's so gentle. I like it.

01:38.420 --> 01:42.220
One of the graduates told me about it.

01:46.500 --> 01:48.350
The title is lovely.

01:48.350 --> 01:49.290
Right?

01:52.370 --> 01:53.630
Wanna play together?

01:54.880 --> 01:55.590
Are you sure?

01:57.960 --> 02:00.770
Shall I bring you a chair?

02:01.690 --> 02:03.380
Kanade-chan!

02:04.190 --> 02:05.470
Huh?

02:06.940 --> 02:09.240
I'm not letting you play without me.

02:09.240 --> 02:13.560
I've been wanting to play it 
with Kumiko-senpai someday.

02:13.910 --> 02:20.000
All the members know you play that piece 
on your own whenever something's wrong.

02:20.560 --> 02:21.490
I do?

02:21.490 --> 02:22.660
Yeah.

02:22.660 --> 02:25.390
I can tell you cherish it.

02:25.390 --> 02:26.630
She does, doesn't she?

02:28.450 --> 02:30.700
Hey, Kumiko-senpai...

02:30.700 --> 02:34.820
Is it all right if I play this 
piece when I'm down, too?

02:36.710 --> 02:40.890
Now, it's your turn to see that the 
underclassmen hear that piece.

02:43.490 --> 02:44.350
Yea.

02:45.480 --> 02:48.030
I want everyone to play it from now on.

02:49.010 --> 02:52.370
<i>I want it to get passed down.</i>

02:53.200 --> 02:55.230
Play it with respect.

02:55.230 --> 02:56.910
It's important to me.

02:57.520 --> 02:58.390
Okay!

02:59.070 --> 03:01.070
<b>Two days prior</b>

03:01.070 --> 03:03.160
Enjoy
<b>Euphonium</b>

03:13.240 --> 03:14.970
About the music school in America...

03:15.470 --> 03:18.560
I'm going to be studying under
an acquaintance of my dad's.

03:18.560 --> 03:19.850
You are, huh?

03:20.460 --> 03:22.110
Are they amazing?

03:22.580 --> 03:23.430
Yeah.

03:26.970 --> 03:37.940
I'm going to study music, learn lots, 
and become as good a performer as my dad.

03:38.960 --> 03:40.310
And when you do?

03:42.280 --> 03:43.530
And when I do...

03:44.850 --> 03:47.500
I plan to confess to Taki-sensei.

03:49.330 --> 03:50.570
Yup, yup.

03:51.140 --> 03:52.130
What's that supposed to mean?

03:52.130 --> 03:55.680
It's just that I was sure you would.

03:57.210 --> 03:58.890
You're gonna have to work hard.

04:00.250 --> 04:01.040
Yeah.

04:01.430 --> 04:04.000
I don't know how many 
years it's going to take.

04:04.630 --> 04:07.270
Taki-sensei might end up a grandpa by then.

04:07.770 --> 04:09.170
I don't care.

04:10.160 --> 04:11.620
I'm serious!

04:11.620 --> 04:13.290
I know you are!

04:19.230 --> 04:20.730
<b>The day before</b>

04:20.740 --> 04:23.270
I love curry!

04:23.270 --> 04:25.690
Don't you get nervous?

04:26.020 --> 04:31.680
We get to present what we've been practicing 
all this time in front of a lot of people.

04:31.680 --> 04:34.700
What could ever be so fun?

04:34.700 --> 04:36.280
Yeah...

04:36.280 --> 04:37.890
You're right.

04:37.890 --> 04:38.580
Yeah.

04:38.980 --> 04:40.640
All right!

04:41.090 --> 04:42.470
Let's do this!

04:42.470 --> 04:43.290
Yeah!

04:43.290 --> 04:45.200
Yeah!

04:46.760 --> 04:48.760
<b>Competition Day</b>

04:56.840 --> 04:59.480
You made it, Oumae-san.

04:59.480 --> 05:00.340
Yes.

05:01.040 --> 05:03.720
Please show us what we didn't get to see.

05:04.130 --> 05:05.750
Leave it to us.

05:06.140 --> 05:08.130
You've come so far.

05:08.130 --> 05:09.340
I knew you would.

05:09.340 --> 05:13.180
It's thanks to what you and 
our other senpais built.

05:13.180 --> 05:14.510
No, uh....

05:14.510 --> 05:15.740
Well, I'll take it.

05:18.010 --> 05:19.860
Okay, well, I should get going.

05:19.860 --> 05:20.740
Yeah.

05:20.740 --> 05:22.090
Go for it.

05:22.090 --> 05:23.070
Yeah.

05:26.090 --> 05:27.720
<b>Performance
order</b>

05:26.370 --> 05:27.720
Kumiko-senpai.

05:28.230 --> 05:30.370
Please have this.

05:29.140 --> 05:31.640
<b>President Kumiko
 Go for it!</b>

05:31.630 --> 05:32.630
I get to have this?

05:32.630 --> 05:33.520
Yes.

05:33.520 --> 05:34.630
This one, too.

05:34.630 --> 05:36.650
It's a charm from Sally's shrine.

05:36.650 --> 05:37.820
Thanks.

05:37.820 --> 05:41.760
I guess the good times are <i>not gone, yeah</i>?

05:41.760 --> 05:43.250
You know, since we're in <i>Nagoya</i>.

05:43.680 --> 05:46.110
I have one, too!

05:46.410 --> 05:47.710
This is a good day

05:47.710 --> 05:49.100
Because now I have received

05:49.100 --> 05:50.040
This omamori

05:50.040 --> 05:51.220
That's a haiku.

05:51.220 --> 05:52.880
Isn't that what we're doing?

05:52.880 --> 05:55.500
Something from you, too, Micchan-senpai!

05:56.430 --> 05:57.800
I hold in my arms

05:57.800 --> 05:59.240
An instrument of music

05:59.240 --> 06:00.250
The color of dreams

06:00.250 --> 06:01.800
That's legit!

06:01.800 --> 06:02.640
That's legit!

06:02.640 --> 06:03.630
Legit!

06:03.630 --> 06:04.630
Actually legit!

06:04.630 --> 06:06.020
That's our Micchan!

06:06.020 --> 06:08.460
This is it, huh?

06:06.020 --> 06:08.570
Now it's Hazuki-senpai's turn, then.

06:08.570 --> 06:11.140
Me? I don't have anything.

06:09.350 --> 06:11.110
I wish you'd smile.

06:11.110 --> 06:13.540
I think you're amazing, Motomu-kun.

06:11.140 --> 06:13.190
Oh, don't say that.

06:13.540 --> 06:16.060
Amazing? I am?

06:16.060 --> 06:18.890
Yes, you're amazing.

06:22.750 --> 06:27.190
I'm glad to have been your senpai.

06:29.370 --> 06:31.180
Thank you.

06:35.090 --> 06:36.570
Kumiko-senpai.

06:37.300 --> 06:40.710
Let me see what Kitauji
looks like at 100 percent.

06:41.110 --> 06:42.240
You bet.

06:45.380 --> 06:47.810
Come on, Suzume, you too.

06:47.810 --> 06:48.850
Okay!

06:48.850 --> 06:50.090
Hug!

06:50.430 --> 06:51.790
What's up with them?

06:51.790 --> 06:53.790
Skinship training.

06:54.220 --> 06:56.860
Oh, right, to show love.

06:58.300 --> 07:00.220
Should we do it, too?

07:07.300 --> 07:08.720
It'll be okay.

07:08.720 --> 07:10.940
You're the best around.

07:13.310 --> 07:16.130
Okay, Kitauji, let's move.

07:16.130 --> 07:17.290
Okay.

07:18.990 --> 07:21.140
Isn't that Taki-sensei?

07:22.370 --> 07:24.500
Shoot, he's so hot.

07:25.100 --> 07:26.350
You don't mind?

07:26.350 --> 07:28.340
I realized lately...

07:28.340 --> 07:30.120
Taki-sensei's just too attractive.

07:30.120 --> 07:32.210
They can't be blamed.

07:32.850 --> 07:33.840
Yeah?

07:34.280 --> 07:34.990
Yeah.

07:37.990 --> 07:41.340
I love Kitauji.

07:39.310 --> 07:41.810
<b>3rd-year Hisae Takano
Clarinet</b>

